>>As with most such cases, the ellipsized x2 has some value less
>> releavnt to the claim, which is consistent with the predication being
>true.
>> In the case of this example, x2 is probably "da".
>
>So why would we not say {lo remna ka'e vofli} meaning that
> {lo remna ka'e vofli lo vinji}?

OK, zo'e then, or da poi co'e at least.  We obviously have a restriction in
mind on thex2 of vofli in that claim.

But of course some might say that the first is true because of the second
because they have a different in mind set of x2 restrictions.

